<zk>
	<label multiline="true">
		A closed groupbox keeps its content in ROD, so the menupopup below has no DOM node at all.
		Opening it has to render the container first instead of replacing a node that does not exist.
		1. Click "open the popup". There should be no error in the console (F12).
		2. The popup shows the two menu items.
	</label>

	<groupbox id="gb" open="false" width="300px">
		<caption label="a closed groupbox"/>
		<menupopup id="mp">
			<menuitem id="mi1" label="a"/>
			<menuitem id="mi2" label="b"/>
		</menupopup>
		<label id="inside" value="content of the groupbox"/>
	</groupbox>

	<button id="op" label="open the popup" popup="mp"/>
</zk>
